# CometGUI -- jpackage options for macOS arm64 (tier 1) and x86-64 (tier 2).
#
# NEVER EXECUTED.  Written in Phase 14, unit 5 on a Linux host: jpackage is
# not a cross-compiler (the Linux JDK's jdk.jpackage module contains no macOS
# bundler), and no macOS machine exists in this environment.  Nothing here has
# been shown to work; Phase 16's macOS runner is the first place it can run.
#
# What is known without running it, from the macOS JDK's own jdk.jpackage
# module and Oracle's JDK 25 packaging guide (docs/feasibility/toolchain.rst,
# "The macOS runner"):
#   * dmg uses /usr/bin/hdiutil; pkg uses pkgbuild and productbuild -- all
#     shipped with macOS.  An unsigned, default-icon dmg needs no Xcode.
#   * Signing (--mac-sign, --mac-signing-key-user-name) needs Developer ID
#     certificates; notarisation is a separate xcrun notarytool step after
#     jpackage.  Both belong to Phase 16 and are not configured here.
#   * LIKELY TO FAIL AS IT STANDS, UNVERIFIED: the macOS bundler is believed to
#     reject an --app-version whose first number is zero (it becomes
#     CFBundleVersion), and this build's version is 0.1.0.  The message is not
#     in the Linux JDK's jdk.jpackage resources, so it could not be checked
#     here.  Recorded rather than worked around: the version is the build
#     identity's (cometgui-app's build-identity.properties), not this file's.
#   * The architecture of the image is the architecture of the JDK running
#     jpackage: an arm64 JDK makes an arm64 .app.  The x86-64 build is a
#     separate run on an x86-64 JDK.
#
# The bundled runtime's module list and the java options are the same as on
# Linux (common.args, packaging/runtime-modules.txt).  No --icon: the project
# has no .icns yet.

--type dmg
--mac-package-identifier org.cometgui.CometGUI
--mac-package-name CometGUI
